.obsidian/
__pycache__/
.venv/
*.pyc

# Toolkit-managed caches. _meta/.cache/ is written by the MCP framework itself:
# fts.db (an SQLite full-text index over every document) and siblings/ (cached
# sibling-corpus indexes for cross-corpus citation resolution). Neither is an
# input to anything — both rebuild on demand — and committing a binary SQLite
# file that changes on every ingest is exactly the kind of repository bloat that
# is painful to undo later.
_meta/.cache/

# corpus-detect-changes writes these to the repo root on every run that reaches
# the fetch loop. Both are a per-run report (what changed, what failed to fetch),
# not an input to anything downstream and not corpus content -- committing them
# would just make every drift run a diff-only commit for its own sake.
changed-sources.tsv
source-outcomes.json

# GitHub Pages build output, if this corpus publishes a site.
site/

# Secret-shaped files. Nothing here should ever produce one, which is precisely
# why these are worth listing: a public civic-data repo gets no second chance
# once a credential is pushed, and the cost of the safety net is three lines.
*.env
.env
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

.DS_Store

# Source PDFs are NOT committed; frontmatter declares snapshot_policy: hash-only.
# The pdftotext extraction (.txt) IS committed — hash_snapshot() hashes its
# normalized text, which is what CI re-verifies. (The oregon-audits arrangement.)
#
# `*.pdf` already covers the OCR pass's derived `<id>.ocr.pdf` copies (ocrmypdf
# writes them beside the original, never over it -- see the OCR policy note in
# src/ingest_counties.py): a gitignore glob segment matches `.` like any other
# character, so it does not stop at the extra dot. Verified 2026-09-12
# (oregon-collective-bargaining#95) with a real `--ocr` run: `git status
# --porcelain _meta/snapshots/` came back clean and `git check-ignore` confirmed
# the produced `.ocr.pdf`. Keep this comment if `*.pdf` is ever narrowed below --
# that is exactly the change that would silently start letting `.ocr.pdf` through.
_meta/snapshots/*.pdf
_meta/snapshots/*.html
_meta/snapshots/*.signed

# Semantic index — built from the corpus and MOUNTED at runtime, never committed
# (_meta/corpus.yml says so under plugins.semantic_search_module; nothing enforced it,
# so a local build landed in `git add -A` staging until it was caught by review).
_meta/embeddings/

# OCR intermediate page renders — PaddleOCR working directory. A previous run
# leaked p-1.png into the repo; these are derived, large, and reproducible.
_meta/snapshots/.paddle-work/
